hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27762","Haddathana Hammad ibn Masada who said: Haddathana Ibn Jurayj from Abu al-Zubayr from Umar ibn Nabhan from Abu Thalaba al-Ashjai who said: I said: Two sons of mine have died for me, O Messenger of Allah, in Islam; so he said: Whoever has two sons die for him in Islam, Allah, mighty and majestic, admits him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy to them; he said: So when it was after that, Abu Hurayra met me; he said: So he said: Are you the one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the two sons what he said; I said: Yes; he said: So he said: If he had said it to me, it would be dearer to me than what Hims and Palestine have enclosed."
